Feature: Inventory Transaction Table (f_inv_movmnt) SQL Logic and Data Mapping

  The system must populate the f_inv_movmnt table in purgo_playground schema using the field mappings and business rules defined in Inventory Txn XPY.xlsx. The logic must ensure correct joins, data transformations, default handling, and error management as per the specification.

  Background:
    Given the following source tables exist in schema purgo_playground:
      | Table   | Columns (partial)                                                                                 |
      | PSEK    | tanpt, pklnr, pjagr, zeipe, dwart, patnr, perks, tgort, ckarg, lzbep, lifdr, sdauf, dunnr, ...   |
      | PCHK    | tanpt, patnr, perks, tgort, ckarg, irsda, ofdat, tumlm, tinsm, peinm, tspem, tlabs, ...          |
      | PARL    | tanpt, patnr, perks, tgort, lmlme, lnsme, linme, spele, lalst, ...                               |
      | PBEV    | patnr, dwkey, xprsv, xtprs, peinl, perpr, ...                                                    |
      | L009T   | perks, tgort, ...                                                                                |
      | PARA    | tanpt, patnr, ptart, ...                                                                         |
      | VBAX    | tanpt, patnr, perks, vpelm, dunnr, ...                                                           |
    And all joins and filters are applied as per the mapping specification
    And all string joins on patnr must use trimmed values
    And the process is a full reload unless otherwise specified

  Scenario Outline: Successful population of f_inv_movmnt with valid source data (Happy Path)
    Given a PSEK record with pklnr="<pklnr>", zeipe="<zeipe>", pjagr="<pjagr>", patnr="<patnr>", perks="<perks>", tgort="<tgort>", dwart="<dwart>", lzbep="<lzbep>", lifdr="<lifdr>", sdauf="<sdauf>", dunnr="<dunnr>"
    And a matching PCHK record with tanpt="<tanpt>", pklnr="<pklnr>", ckarg="<ckarg>", tumlm=<tumlm>, tinsm=<tinsm>, peinm=<peinm>, tspem=<tspem>, tlabs=<tlabs>, irsda="<irsda>", ofdat="<ofdat>"
    And a matching PARL record with perks="<perks>", tgort="<tgort>", lmlme=<lmlme>, lnsme=<lnsme>, linme=<linme>, spele=<spele>, lalst=<lalst>
    And a matching PBEV record with patnr="<patnr>", dwkey="<perks>", xprsv="<xprsv>", xtprs=<xtprs>, peinl=<peinl>, perpr=<perpr>
    And a matching PARA record with tanpt="<tanpt>", patnr="<patnr>", ptart="<ptart>"
    And a matching L009T record with perks="<perks>", tgort="<tgort>"
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then a record is inserted into f_inv_movmnt with:
      | txn_id                | "<pklnr>|<zeipe>|<pjagr>"                                 |
      | inv_loc               | "<tgort>"                                                |
      | financial_qty         | <expected_financial_qty>                                 |
      | net_qty               | <expected_net_qty>                                       |
      | expired_dt            | "<expected_expired_dt>"                                  |
      | item_nbr              | "<patnr>"                                                |
      | unit_cost             | <expected_unit_cost>                                     |
      | uom_rate              | 0.76                                                     |
      | plant_loc_cd          | "<perks>"                                                |
      | inv_stock_reference   | "<expected_inv_stock_reference>"                         |
      | stock_type            | "<expected_stock_type>"                                  |
      | qty_on_hand           | <expected_net_qty>                                       |
      | qty_shipped           | <expected_financial_qty> - <expected_net_qty>            |
      | cancel_dt             | null                                                     |
      | flag_active           | "<expected_flag_active>"                                 |
      | crt_dt                | current timestamp                                        |
      | updt_dt               | current timestamp                                        |
    And all values conform to the data types and formats specified

    Examples:
      | pklnr | zeipe | pjagr | patnr   | perks | tgort | dwart | lzbep | lifdr   | sdauf   | dunnr   | tanpt | ckarg | tumlm | tinsm | peinm | tspem | tlabs | irsda     | ofdat     | lmlme | lnsme | linme | spele | lalst | xprsv | xtprs | peinl | perpr | ptart | expected_financial_qty | expected_net_qty | expected_expired_dt | expected_unit_cost | expected_inv_stock_reference | expected_stock_type | expected_flag_active |
      | 1001  | 01    | 200   | ABC123  | PL01  | L001  | AA    | B     | SUPP001 |         |         | T01   | X1    | 10    | 5     | 2     | 1     | 0.5   | 20240601   | 20240610  | 8     | 4     | 1     | 0.5   | 0.2   | S     | 100   | 2     | 200   | FERT  | 18.5                  | 18.5             | 20240610            | 50.00              | SUPP001                    | FG                 | yes                 |
      | 1002  | 02    | 201   | XYZ789  | PL02  | L002  | BB    | L     |         | ORD001  |         | T02   |       |       |       |       |       |       | 20240602   | 20240611  | 7     | 3     | 2     | 0.3   | 0.1   | V     | 0     | 1     | 100   | ROH   | 12.4                  | 12.4             | 20240611            | 100.00             | <VBAX_DUNNR>                | RAW                | yes                 |

  Scenario: Default value handling for missing inv_loc
    Given a PSEK record with tgort as null
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the inv_loc field in f_inv_movmnt is set to "none"

  Scenario: Default value handling for missing financial_qty
    Given no matching PCHK or PARL records for a PSEK record
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the financial_qty field in f_inv_movmnt is set to 0

  Scenario: Default value handling for missing net_qty
    Given no matching PCHK or PARL records for a PSEK record
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the net_qty field in f_inv_movmnt is set to 0

  Scenario: Default value handling for missing expired_dt
    Given no matching PCHK record for a PSEK record
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the expired_dt field in f_inv_movmnt is set to "99991231"

  Scenario: Default value handling for missing unit_cost
    Given no matching PBEV record for a PSEK record
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the unit_cost field in f_inv_movmnt is set to null

  Scenario: Default value handling for missing uom_rate
    Given any PSEK record
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the uom_rate field in f_inv_movmnt is set to 0.76

  Scenario: Default value handling for missing plant_loc_cd
    Given a PSEK record with perks as null
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the plant_loc_cd field in f_inv_movmnt is set to "none"

  Scenario Outline: inv_stock_reference logic for LZBEP and related fields
    Given a PSEK record with lzbep="<lzbep>", lifdr="<lifdr>", dunnr="<dunnr>", sdauf="<sdauf>"
    And a matching VBAX record with vpelm="<sdauf>", dunnr="<vbax_dunnr>"
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the inv_stock_reference field in f_inv_movmnt is set to "<expected_inv_stock_reference>"

    Examples:
      | lzbep | lifdr   | dunnr   | sdauf   | vbax_dunnr | expected_inv_stock_reference |
      | B     | SUPP001 |         |         |            | SUPP001                      |
      | B     |         |         |         |            | none                         |
      | L     |         | DUN001  |         |            | DUN001                       |
      | L     |         |         | ORD001  | VBAXSUPP   | VBAXSUPP                     |
      | L     |         |         |         |            | none                         |
      | X     |         |         |         |            | none                         |

  Scenario Outline: stock_type mapping from PARA.ptart
    Given a PARA record with ptart="<ptart>"
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the stock_type field in f_inv_movmnt is set to "<expected_stock_type>"

    Examples:
      | ptart | expected_stock_type |
      | FERT  | FG                 |
      | ROH   | RAW                |
      | HALB  | WIP                |
      | NULL  | OT                 |
      | ABC   | OT                 |

  Scenario: qty_on_hand equals net_qty
    Given a calculated net_qty value of 15.5
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the qty_on_hand field in f_inv_movmnt is set to 15.5

  Scenario: qty_shipped calculation
    Given a calculated financial_qty of 20 and net_qty of 15
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the qty_shipped field in f_inv_movmnt is set to 5

  Scenario: cancel_dt logic for missing mantr in current data
    Given a record present in yesterday's data but not in today's data
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the cancel_dt field in f_inv_movmnt is set to today's date in yyyymmdd format

  Scenario Outline: flag_active logic based on dwart
    Given a PSEK record with dwart="<dwart>"
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the flag_active field in f_inv_movmnt is set to "<expected_flag_active>"

    Examples:
      | dwart | expected_flag_active |
      | RX    | no                  |
      | TX    | no                  |
      | PX    | no                  |
      | AA    | yes                 |
      | null  | no                  |

  Scenario: Null and default handling for all fields
    Given a PSEK record with all nullable fields as null
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then all fields in f_inv_movmnt are set to their default values as per the mapping

  Scenario: Uniqueness constraint on txn_id
    Given two PSEK records with the same pklnr, zeipe, and pjagr
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then only one record with that txn_id is inserted into f_inv_movmnt

  Scenario: Error handling for duplicate source records in joins
    Given multiple PCHK records matching the same PSEK record
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then only the first PCHK record ordered by irsda DESC is used for expired_dt

  Scenario: Error handling for data type mismatches
    Given a source value for financial_qty that cannot be cast to double
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the record is rejected and an error is logged with message "Invalid data type for financial_qty"

  Scenario: Error handling for missing required item_nbr
    Given a PSEK record with patnr as null
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the record is rejected and an error is logged with message "item_nbr (patnr) is required"

  Scenario: Validation of output data
    Given the f_inv_movmnt table is populated
    When the data is validated
    Then all records must:
      | Field         | Validation Rule                                                                 |
      | txn_id        | Not null, unique, format "<pklnr>|<zeipe>|<pjagr>"                              |
      | inv_loc       | Not null, string, "none" if missing                                            |
      | financial_qty | Not null, double, 0 if missing                                                 |
      | net_qty       | Not null, double, 0 if missing                                                 |
      | expired_dt    | Not null, yyyymmdd, "99991231" if missing                                      |
      | item_nbr      | Not null, string                                                               |
      | unit_cost     | double, rounded to 2 decimal places, null if missing                           |
      | uom_rate      | Not null, double, always 0.76                                                  |
      | plant_loc_cd  | Not null, string, "none" if missing                                            |
      | inv_stock_reference | string, "none" if missing                                                |
      | stock_type    | Not null, one of [RAW, WIP, FG, OT]                                            |
      | qty_on_hand   | Not null, double, equals net_qty                                               |
      | qty_shipped   | Not null, double, equals financial_qty - net_qty, 0 if negative                |
      | cancel_dt     | yyyymmdd or null                                                               |
      | flag_active   | Not null, "yes" or "no"                                                        |
      | crt_dt        | Not null, timestamp                                                            |
      | updt_dt       | Not null, timestamp                                                            |

  Scenario: Join precedence and order
    Given all joins are defined as per the mapping
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then joins are applied in the following order:
      | Order | Join Description                                                                                 |
      | 1     | left join pchk on pchk.TANPT = PSEK.TANPT AND pchk.PKLNR = PSEK.PKLNR                           |
      | 2     | left join parl on psek.perks = parl.perks                                                       |
      | 3     | left join PBEV on trim(psek.patnr) = trim(pbev.patnr) and psek.perks = pbev.dwkey               |
      | 4     | left join L009T on parl.perks = l009t.perks and parl.tgort = l009t.tgort                        |
      | 5     | left join para on pchk.tanpt = para.tanpt and pchk.patnr = para.patnr                           |
      | 6     | left join VBAX to parl on vbax.tanpt = parl.tanpt AND vbax.patnr = parl.patnr AND vbax.perks = parl.perks |

  Scenario: Data volume and performance
    Given the source tables contain more than 1 million records each
    When the SQL logic is executed
    Then the process completes within the defined SLA and does not cause timeouts or memory errors

  Scenario: Orchestration and triggering
    Given the SQL logic is deployed in the data platform
    When the scheduled job is triggered
    Then the f_inv_movmnt table is refreshed as a full load

  Scenario: Relationship with *_apl_qty tables
    Given the f_inv_movmnt table is populated
    When the *_apl_qty tables are populated
    Then the txn_id values in *_apl_qty tables must reference existing txn_id values in f_inv_movmnt

  Scenario: Null/default propagation to *_apl_qty tables
    Given a txn_id in f_inv_movmnt with default/null values for optional fields
    When the corresponding *_apl_qty record is created
    Then the *_apl_qty record is created with the same txn_id and appropriate default/null values for its fields

